    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] This battle should not be confused with the Day of Zamora (\"Día de Zamora\" or \"Jornada del Foso de Zamora\") which took place a few decades before in the year 901.\n[2] The Battle of Hürtgen Forest (German: \"Schlacht im Hürtgenwald\" ) was a series of fierce battles fought from 19 September to 16 December 1944 between American and German forces on the Western Front during World War II in the Hürtgen Forest about 50 mi2 east of the Belgian–German border.\n[3] The Battle of Gettysburg ( , with an sound) was fought July 1–3, 1863, in and around the town of Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, by Union and Confederate forces during the American Civil War.\n[4] It is set during the World War II Battle of Hürtgen Forest in Autumn of 1944."
